.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:3:Status: **FORMAL STEPS OPEN / NOT YET CONTROLLER-SIGNED**. This is a TRAIN-only pre-freeze package. The real-anchor compute gate passed before the formal manifests, allocation, calibration, rehearsal and development smoke were opened. No TEST data or claim-panel outcome was opened. The ten-anchor smoke is diagnostic and cannot establish admission.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:18:The v1.9 margin implementation preserves nominal predicted/executed power and nominal interferers. A sealed 200,000-draw cached quantile of the complete fading product affects only wanted-link predicted reception and transmitted-mode choice. ACM emits `m_target`, `m_tx` and realised decode outcome separately and credits the transmitted mode only on a realised threshold pass. Selection-time and realised endpoint decompositions remain separate; every coalition receives its interaction label, while Shapley attribution alone is capped at four users.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:26:On three real quarantined a-r0 decisions, catalogue counts were 997, 997 and 966. Decision times were 9.920572, 8.879807 and 5.949833 s: mean 8.250071 s, p95 9.816495 s, maximum 9.920572 s. Complete-anchor totals were 21.315449, 20.119099 and 20.540675 s: mean 20.658408 s, p95 21.237972 s. Thus both the <10 s selection and <60 s per-anchor gates pass. Provider construction was 20.222051 s once/world.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:57:The authoritative schema-corrected rehearsal is `.tmp/stage4h-formal-q/rehearsal.json`: 3 anchors, 14 arms, 15,566 physical boundary evaluations, 67.030349 s and 4.468690 four-worker core-minutes. `q=0.013688590926973465`. File SHA-256: `06d6a0dd292b6ac7f37efe47bf0fccccb8f56fa39395a7f0a2b7e584d701fcf7`; unit receipt: `3090021b89e254c0cbc45ad53fc77dc6d1e0696a40698e8e4fb23d08a7338f03`.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:59:The direct 4×90-anchor projection is 8.937380 core-hours. At process concurrency 20 and four workers/unit, five units run concurrently and ideal projected wall time is 26.812140 minutes. The rehearsal is below 10 core-minutes and the projection is below 160 core-hours, so the smallest sealed anchor stride is `k=1`; no thinning rung is invoked.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:63:The 10-anchor, 14-arm run is explicitly `SMOKE_NOT_MATRIX`: `.tmp/stage4h-formal/smoke/a-r0-world-1.json`, file SHA-256 `f772877da8fb2fcd45d626c92a3bf8725fc47326c90ad8529977cac0695dceed`, receipt `a39b0c174118374bfb04640affed08e80b243d1f4b28353fa42e038cb42e82d9`. It used 15.535257 core-minutes. The full arm table, causal ACM census, factor marginals, `g_A/g_I`, availability, lit-beam time, cap/plateau shares and certificate distributions are in `../V025-ENGINE-STAGE4H-REPORT-2026-09-09.md` and the immutable receipt.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/SEAL-PACKAGE-DRAFT-2026-09-08.md:65:Paired ACM before/after evidence is `.tmp/stage4h/acm-before-after.json` (receipt `5fa975a282bfb319933ab01eb31c0430c0af904987d05593b53c3efdfd48e2c9`). The corrected two-anchor availability is 0.453138 and pooled EE 5.658947 Mbit/J, down from genie values 0.791277 and 18.940246 Mbit/J at identical energy.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COUPLED-SOLVE-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **KATs.** (a) a 3-user fixture with spectral radius 0.999 converges within budget to the analytic fixed point; (b) a fixture where two users' targets are jointly unattainable certifies `CONVERGED` with both at cap and `rate_target_infeasible`; (c) an injected NaN yields `INVALID` and stops; (d) the real-world rehearsal on the quarantined world 1 evaluates BASE:nearest-eligible without error and reports the certificate distribution over anchors.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/QUANTILE-SWEEP-SMOKE-2026-09-09.md:5:The sweep uses the common exogenous tape `V025_SMOKE/world/1`, two carried decision anchors, all 14 arms, four declared evaluation workers, the sealed one-boundary/M=48 selection fallback, and the ordinary realised 48-boundary committed endpoint. Each arm carries its own configuration and served-user state; calls are deduplicated only while both states are identical. Deadline misses and BASE fallbacks remain in the outcomes.
