.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Executable set-score decomposition (from the review's pass 1(d)).** For a configuration with changed-user set A relative to the anchor reference a⁰ and F = B − η_ref·E: unilateral increments dᵢ = F(aᵢ, a⁰₋ᵢ) − F(a⁰); interaction residual Ψ_A = F(a_A, a⁰₋A) − F(a⁰) − Σᵢ∈A dᵢ. C1(config) = Σᵢ∈A dᵢ (+ Φ), C3(config) = Ψ_A (credited to users by the Shapley allocation of the interaction game; pairs = Ψ/2 each), C2(config) = the declared continuation value excluding the immediate term. Identity: C1 + C3 = F(a_A) − F(a⁰) exactly (KAT). Factor arms: FULL = C1 + C2 + C3; DROP_C1 = C2 + C3; DROP_C2 = C1 + C3; DROP_C3 = C1 + C2 (additive), all in the same selector class and catalogue (stage-4 item 18).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **C3-SET-REPRESENTATION** — set head input = permutation-invariant pooling (sum and max) over the changed users' per-user vectors (their Q1 row for the selected action, their incumbent row, `missing_incumbent`), concatenated with global resource context per affected beam (occupancy before/after, activation change, interference summary, cap margin), padded to |A| ≤ 4 with masks; a two-layer MLP on the pooled vector; anchored zeros by construction (output × 𝟙[|A| ≥ 2]). Shapley for reporting: exact over subsets for |A| ≤ 4.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:12:8. **DEADLINE-CLOCK** — wall clock (monotonic) on `sat`; coordinator worker count = 4 processes; no warm caches for decision timing (cold per anchor); the timing evidence is the per-phase table of stage 4c.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:13:9. **FORMAL-ALLOCATION** — at seal, by the assembler (worlds, dates, starts, seeds, 30-anchor coverage, stride, manifest digest).
