.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 — controller decisions after the stage-4c real-anchor gate (2026-09-08 ≈ 21:50 UTC; before any formal successor outcome)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:3:Trigger: stage 4c stopped at the mandatory real-anchor gate: the a-r0 FULL selector on the quarantined world chose a 100-user coalition; the runner then tried an exact Shapley validation over 2^100 subsets and failed closed; the timing table read catalogue 3.0 s, stage 1 36.5 s, stage-2 forecasts 17.8 s, selection 0.01 s — 59.7 s to failure against the 10 s selection budget.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Selection-time grid:** stage-1 immediate scores are computed at the decision instant only (k = 0; the deployable controller's own view), stage-2 continuation for the top-M = 64 at the 5-boundary grid, the committed profile and all labels/endpoint at 48 boundaries (unchanged). KAT: the endpoint of a committed profile is bit-identical before/after; report the top-1 agreement between k = 0 scoring and the 5-boundary scoring on the rehearsal anchors.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Budget arithmetic (to verify at the gate):** ≈ 1 200 rows × 0.0014 s ≈ 1.7 s stage 1; 64 × 3 offsets × 5 boundaries batched ≈ 2 s; catalogue 3 s; selection + validation < 1 s → ≈ 7 s selection, well under 10 s; per anchor total (with 48-boundary commit of ≤ 14 arms) ≤ 60 s.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Reference state note (physics finding, not a change):** with the nearest-eligible carrier as a⁰ under rate-target physics, nearly every arm reassigns most users; the meaningful headroom comparisons are against U_all / S_UNI (unilateral local optimum) and S0, which the arm set contains. The carriers stay as sealed.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-4C-GATE-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Gate:** if the real anchor still misses the 10 s selection budget after items 1–3, stop and report the dominating phase; no further approximation without a controller decision.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **B2 — factor arms cannot measure component marginals (design CHANGE).** The set decoder's score for FULL/DROP arms is the **sum of the declared targets**, not the exact realised objective: S(config) = C1(config) + C2(config) + C3(config), each the declared target in bits computed by the oracle from the same nominal physics (C1 whole-network difference surplus + Φ; C2 three-offset forecasts with −κ; C3 = interaction share per decision item 5 / Shapley for sets). DROP_Cx removes exactly one term inside the **same selector class and the same catalogue**; `DROP_C3` = no interaction term (joint search kept); an additional `UNI` arm = unilateral-only search with all three terms is reported separately (search value ≠ interaction value); `S_UNI` (stage-4 item 11) is the iterated exact-unilateral comparator. The exact-F oracle is a **ceiling arm** (U1/J1/union certificates), never a factor arm. Marginals are measured on the realised pooled endpoint ΣB/ΣE, never on nominal scores. KATs: on a synthetic world with a constructed non-zero interaction, FULL and DROP_C3 select different configurations and the realised marginal equals the hand-computed value; with zero interaction they coincide; DROP_C1/DROP_C2 differ from FULL on fixtures where the dropped term is decisive.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:3:Source: provider v1 report — with the Python-object tape, the 57 525-chain cross-product inventory and the unbatched runner, the measured cost is 12.63 s per anchor of provider acquisition, 4.66 s per 48-boundary catalogue row, q ≈ 0.308, ≈ 182 868 core-hours for the plan (budget: 160). This is an engineering failure of the current implementation, not a property of the physics; the decisions below fix the implementation first and only then thin the plan, in a pre-declared order.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Engineering targets (stage 4, before any thinning):** dense per-step numpy tapes (provider decision 9); realisable inventory only (≈ 2 760 chains, decision 4/D4); batched evaluation of a whole catalogue per anchor — the capped fixed point, ACM lookup, energy and bits computed for all configurations of an anchor in one vectorised pass over (configuration × boundary); provider acquisition amortised once per world (48 × 30 boundaries computed once and shared by all settings and arms). Target: ≤ 0.02 s per catalogue row per anchor and ≤ 1 s per anchor of provider work on the reference hardware; the rehearsal reports both.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Catalogue size cap (decision 4 refined):** pairwise joint moves are restricted to the top-K = 10 users by nominal unilateral surplus **and their top-2 legal options each** (≤ 45 × 4 = 180 rows); unilateral rows ≤ users × legal options (≈ 2 700); evacuation sets ≤ active beams (≈ 40); S0 proposals ≤ 200. Catalogue ≤ ≈ 3 200 rows per anchor.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Reporting:** the rehearsal writes a cost table (per world: provider seconds; per anchor: rows, seconds; projection per setting) into the seal package; the projection and the applied thinning steps are sealed before the first unit opens.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:6:1. **Producer:** tapes (provider decisions 9–11) → per (anchor, user, legal action) rows built by one production builder; every row carries world/user/action/time/calibration lineage; TRAIN-only asserted at construction.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Labels:** C1 whole-network surplus + Φ (bits / κ); C2 three-offset forecast core with −κ per absorbing lost offset (bits / κ); C3 interaction share only (Ψ/2 pairs; Shapley for sets) over the sealed bounded catalogue; κ per stage-4 item 24; all prices explicit.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:16:9. **Deployed selector:** per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2 sum (bits / κ) for the two-head policy; the C3 layer is the set-level coordinator (learned S3 or exact S0) over the bounded catalogue with the sealed service guard, a 30.08 s deadline, BASE-proposal fallback, and the deployment-capability manifest (stage-4 item 26); the information-matched `S_UNI` comparator is always evaluated beside it.
