.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:3:Trigger: stage-4 real-world measurements on the quarantined world — 2 800 legal candidates, 2 912 catalogue rows per anchor, 0.0335 s per row for the exact 48-boundary immediate score, C2 forecasts unbatched (> 450 s per anchor), provider one-step construction 9.9–12.5 s. A complete anchor is far beyond the coordinator's own decision budget, so the exact-everything selector is not a deployable object either. The physics, labels and endpoint stay exact at 48 boundaries; **selection-time scoring** gets the approximations a real controller would use. All values below are sealed before any outcome; none may be changed after.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Catalogue shortlist (replaces the "all legal options" unilateral set):** per user, the top-8 legal options by nominal single-link decoding margin at the decision instant (deployable shortlist) → ≤ 800 unilateral rows; pairwise among the top-10 users by exact nominal unilateral surplus × their top-2 options (≤ 180); per-active-beam evacuations (≈ 40); S0 top-two + evacuations (≤ 200). Catalogue ≈ 1 200 rows. The stage-3 item-10 diagnostic reports, per anchor, how many legal options fall outside the shortlist and the best excluded option's margin.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Coarse selection grid:** selection-time immediate scores use 5 boundaries k ∈ {0, 12, 24, 36, 47} with trapezoid weights over the 30.08 s step; the committed profile, every label (C1/C2/C3) and the endpoint use all 48 boundaries. Report (no gate): top-1 agreement between the 5-boundary and 48-boundary scores on the synthetic and rehearsal anchors.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Two-stage scoring:** stage 1 = immediate score C1 + Ψ (interaction) for all catalogue rows on the coarse grid; stage 2 = C2 continuation (three offsets, batched) only for the top-M = 64 rows by stage-1 score plus BASE, the incumbents and every S0 proposal; the selected profile is the argmax of the complete score within that set. M is sealed.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Batched forecasts:** the three-offset continuation for the stage-2 set is one shared batch call per anchor (configuration × offset × boundary).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Provider amortisation:** the world tape (33 steps × 48 boundaries) is constructed once per world and reused by all arms and settings; construction time is reported per world (≈ 7 min at the measured rate is acceptable); the per-anchor provider target of 1 s is withdrawn in favour of "once per world".
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Budget arithmetic (to be confirmed by the rehearsal):** ≈ 1 200 rows × (5/48) × 0.0335 s ≈ 4.2 s + 64 × 3 offsets ≈ 6 s + selection ≈ 11 s per anchor; a-r0 = 4 worlds × 90 anchors × 13 arms sharing the catalogue ≈ 1–2 core-hours; stride k = 1 expected; the sealed thinning order applies only if the rehearsal disagrees.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:11:7. **Deadline consistency:** the 10 s compute budget (contract v1 §F2) is evaluated against the measured per-anchor time on the declared worker count; a miss executes the validated BASE.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:12:8. **KATs:** shortlist superset report field; 5- vs 48-boundary agreement report; two-stage argmax equals the full-catalogue argmax on synthetic anchors where the true optimum is in the top-M (and the miss is reported when it is not); batched forecasts equal per-row forecasts to 1e-9.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **World duration / anchors** — **CHANGE**: a unit is not three isolated instants. Each fixed carrier (nearest-eligible, stay-if-possible, random-masked) is rolled for the 30 canonical steps and **every step is a decision instant** (30 anchors per carrier, 90 per world, as in the earlier oracle probe), each with its three-offset forecast steps. If the server-provider rehearsal projects more than 160 core-hours, thin by taking every k-th step with the smallest integer k that brings the projection under budget, chosen from the projection before any unit outcome is opened, and record k in the seal.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Catalogue census** — **CHANGE** for real worlds: the complete Cartesian product of legal assignments is used only when it has ≤ 4 096 configurations (synthetic worlds). Otherwise the union catalogue is the bounded set: (i) every unilateral move of every user to every legal option; (ii) the S0 deployable proposals (top-two per user) and all frozen beam evacuations; (iii) all pairwise joint moves among the top-K = 10 users ranked by nominal unilateral surplus, over all their legal option pairs; (iv) per-active-beam evacuation sets (every user of the beam to its best legal alternative). J1 = the best changed-user-count > 1 configuration in this catalogue; U1 = the best in (i). The catalogue definition and its digest are sealed; the per-world superset check of stage-3 item 10 reports how many legal options fall outside the shortlist.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **LC-SRS e_i binding** — **CHANGE**: under the sealed whole-network C1 (which already contains every unilateral bit and joule change of the network), the unilateral externality e_i is inside C1, so the successor C3 target carries **no e_i term**: z₃,ᵢ = Ψ/2 for pairs and the equal-share (Shapley) split of the set interaction for larger sets, with Ψ computed on F = B − η_ref·E per regime (per-cell re-optimisation). This is the round-6 no-double-counting rule; the historical LC-SRS e_i (defined for an own-bits-only C1) is not transferred.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **QoS guard margins** — **CHANGE** (numeric, prospective): FULL is QoS non-inferior to a DROP arm when the 95 % cluster-bootstrap interval of (FULL − DROP) lies above −0.5 pp for complete-service availability, and the interval of the relative change lies below +5 % for both the handover rate and the Φ-priced handover cost per user-step. Catalogue/service exclusion thresholds do not exclude configurations; they score and report (the service guard used by the deployable decoder is the sealed one from C3-S: no served-count decrease versus the BASE proposal).
